$ crystod-group --poscar2cif -c 225_PPOSCAR_NaCl   # writes the CIF read by the next step

* Structure *
input      : 225_PPOSCAR_NaCl
space group: Fm-3m (No. 225), tolerance 0.01
192 symmetry operations, 2 independent sites

* Output files *
  Bilbao-style CIF written to: 225_PPOSCAR_NaCl.cif

$ crystod-group --cif2poscar -c 225_PPOSCAR_NaCl.cif --conventional --output 225_PPOSCAR_NaCl_conventional   # F-centred: 8-atom conventional cell

* Structure *
input      : 225_PPOSCAR_NaCl.cif
space group: Fm-3m (No. 225), tolerance 0.01
conventional cell, 8 atoms

* Output files *
  POSCAR written to: 225_PPOSCAR_NaCl_conventional

# Axis settings of the space group (crystod-group --cif-axis, --cif2poscar --spacegroup-set);
# testsuite section 22. The table lists every setting (Hall symbol) with the
# lattice parameters of the input cell in its axes, as VESTA's Setting list;
# --spacegroup-set writes the conventional cell of one setting.

$ crystod-group --cif-axis -c POSCAR_La3Ni2O7_Cmcm.cif

